From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 22:15:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] usb: typec: tipd: cd321x: keep the USB link of a
 partner that completes PD

A partner that attaches without PD, or before its identity is read, and
then completes the negotiation reads to cd321x_update_work() as a
different partner: the PD flag or the identity changed while the plug
stayed in. The work then tears the partner down and registers it again,
which resets the mux and drops the USB link the partner already has.

cd321x_partner_completed() (cd321x-dp.h, with its KUnit cases) tells
that case apart from a real change of partner. Use it: a partner that
only completed PD keeps its link, and its port data is refreshed in
place.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/usb/typec/tipd/core.c | 14 +++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/typec/tipd/core.c b/drivers/usb/typec/tipd/core.c
index a43e56d311..2bea28e940 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/tipd/core.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/tipd/core.c
@@ -1168,7 +1168,15 @@ static void cd321x_update_work(struct work_struct *work)
 	bool identity_late = old_connected && new_connected && is_pd &&
 		cd321x->cur_partner_is_pd &&
 		!cd321x_identity_known(&cd321x->cur_partner_identity);
-	bool new_partner = old_connected && new_connected &&
+	/* The same partner completing PD keeps its USB link: refresh it only. */
+	bool partner_completed = old_connected && new_connected &&
+		cd321x_partner_completed(cd321x->cur_partner_is_pd, is_pd,
+					 memchr_inv(&cd321x->cur_partner_identity, 0,
+						    sizeof(cd321x->cur_partner_identity)),
+					 memchr_inv(&st.partner_identity, 0,
+						    sizeof(st.partner_identity)),
+					 reset, st.data_status_changed);
+	bool new_partner = old_connected && new_connected && !partner_completed &&
 		(is_pd != cd321x->cur_partner_is_pd ||
 		 (is_pd && !identity_late &&
 		  memcmp(&st.partner_identity, &cd321x->cur_partner_identity,
@@ -1239,8 +1247,8 @@ static void cd321x_update_work(struct work_struct *work)
 			goto retry;
 	}
 
-	/* Process partner disconnection or change */
-	if (!new_connected || partner_changed) {
+	/* Process partner disconnection or change, or refresh a completed one */
+	if (!new_connected || partner_changed || partner_completed) {
 		if (tps->partner_altmode_dp) {
 			typec_altmode_update_active(tps->partner_altmode_dp, false);
 			typec_unregister_altmode(tps->partner_altmode_dp);
-- 
